  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1227 PM CDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nWednesday currently looks dry across the region as weak upper level \nridging briefly builds overhead, with temperatures also set to warm \nnear or back above seasonal normals. Things already begin to \nchange on Thursday though, as deepening cyclonic flow aloft over \nthe western CONUS focuses a series of southern stream disturbances\nover our region through the rest of the week. Models remain very \nconsistent tracking the first of these waves overhead during the \nlate week period, with chances for widespread showers and storms \narriving late Thursday and continuing through at least Friday. \nModel spread increases thereafter, resulting in increased forecast\nuncertainty heading into the weekend. Even so, consensus still \nfavors continuation of a generally unsettled pattern with rain \nchances persisting through the weekend.",
